  "findings": "Compared spring white umbels on bare scapes and woodland basal leaf carpet photographs with current revised seeds 1/4/7 and every variant in the 36 sheet. Replaced crowded generic rosette stems and oversized white petal rings with separate bulb positions, two broad basal leaves per bulb, bare scapes and seven small flowers on explicit radiating pedicels. Late-spring flowering clumps span approximately 0.25-0.50 m. Small umbels still merge adjacent flower cells at 25 mm; the larger pilots show separate white tips, and true six-part tiny flowers cannot be resolved. Source accepted for the stylized spring forest floor; not yet user endorsed.",
